From cd67c8d9a32e4ba9c41cdb9e34848ef6be025f2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:13:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: a pair drawn over in the source transport is
 converted once, through the GPU's quad operations

Pass 4 of the source transport (PACK, and PACK_GUI where the GUI is read in place) made the codes of
an odd pixel from what was drawn over it and, for the chroma of its pair, made the even pixel's
picture again (the GUI composite, or a fetch of pass 3) and converted it again: a pair drawn over
cost three or four conversions instead of two. Where fragment shaders have the quad operations of
GL_KHR_shader_subgroup, the odd pixel now takes the even pixel's two chroma codes, and whether
anything is drawn over it, from the invocation next to it (subgroupQuadSwapHorizontal), tagged with
the raster position they are of; where the neighbour is not its even pixel it makes them as before.
The same expressions on the same values: the same bytes.

- PACK keeps its program as written for frames with nothing drawn over them; the quad form is a
  program of its own, used only for frames with a layer.
- Both forms are made at the packer's creation, with the form as written as the fallback wherever
  the quad form does not compile, link or has every uniform. dvbridge_source_quad() and
  dvbridge_render_source_quad() say which were made.
- The reference of a check of the bytes (dvbridge_renderer_create_reference()) packs without quad
  operations, as it does with the converted transport's packer, so a check on hardware compares the
  two forms; dvbridge_renderer_create_plain() makes a renderer so, to measure the difference.
- dvbridge_gl_fragment_quad(): the query of the converted transport's packer, made public.

Bytes, host (packed 3840x2160 frames hashed, 6 pictures each of a profile 7 FEL stream, its base
layer alone, and HDR10+ sent as Dolby Vision; the GUI read in place and composited first, a GUI with
a band, an alpha gradient, single-pixel lines, black and opaque panels): 18 of 18 cases identical on
llvmpipe (no quad operations) and zink (quad operations in both forms). Mutants: the chroma codes
swapped, the even pixel's alpha taken from the odd one, the fallback reading the odd pixel's own
composite (with the fallback forced) all change the bytes; the fallback forced gives the same bytes;
the reference made with quad operations is seen.

GPU time of the packing on zink (relative, software): GUI over half the raster read in place 93.6 to
65.2 ms (FEL) and 108.0 to 74.7 (HDR10+ as DV); a band of 300 rows 72.5 to 53.6, base layer alone
77.2 to 56.7; composited first 57.4 to 49.7; nothing drawn over 16.4 and 16.5 (unchanged).

The idea of handing a pair's value through the quad is that of CroqueMr's composite of the GUI
(CB1_GUI_QUAD in his cb1_composite_glsl.h).
